From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:21:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: reserve the pins
 stock reserves

Stock reserves GPIO 36-43, 74, 119, 120 and 144-147 (qcom,gpios-reserved);
the board file reserved only 36-39. Nothing here uses the other eleven
pins. Reserve them too, so that Linux never drives or reconfigures pins
that stock leaves to the secure world.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index f2c3acb8be5d..df2ac127ba99 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1939,7 +1939,8 @@ wcd_tx: codec@0,3 {
 };
 
 &tlmm {
-	gpio-reserved-ranges = <36 4>;
+	/* stock's qcom,gpios-reserved: 36-43, 74, 119, 120, 144-147 */
+	gpio-reserved-ranges = <36 8>, <74 1>, <119 2>, <144 4>;
 
 	/* the pogo data line as a GPIO: low = a dock is attached and unpowered or asleep (stock uart_wake_gpio) */
 	pogo_detect_default: pogo-detect-default-state {
-- 
2.43.0

